          "title": "You'll want to know: راه حل",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "راه حل (râh-e hall) — \"a solution\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "برای این مشکل یک راه حل ساده پیدا کردیم. barâye in moshkel yek râh-e hall-e sâde peydâ kardim. We found a simple solution to this problem."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Râh \"way\" + ezafe + hall \"solving\". Plural râh-e hallhâ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "راه حل (râh-e hall) is literally \"the way of solving\": râh \"road, way\" is inherited Persian (EtymDB traces it back through Proto-Iranian), and hall \"solving\" comes from Arabic ḥall."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
