          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اهمیت داشتن (ahamiyat dâshtan) — \"to matter, to be important\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "برای من نظر تو اهمیت دارد. barâye man nazar-e to ahamiyat dârad. Your opinion matters to me."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ahamiyyat \"importance\" + dâshtan. Ahamiyyat nadârad — it doesn't matter."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اهمیت is usually traced to Arabic ahammiyya \"importance\", from the same Arabic family as mohem \"important\"; dâshtan \"to have\" is the inherited Persian verb."
            }
          ]
        },
